      "side": "Anglo-Portuguese",
      "summary": "The bulk of Wellesley's army, which pinned Delaborde in front. The 29th, pushing too far up a gully, was caught and its colonel killed, but the attack carried the heights.",
      "notes": [
        "Fane's light brigade was riflemen only, the 5/60th and four companies of the 2/95th, with no Line battalions for the list's Infantry Brigade; that shows as a historical departure.",
        "The 6th Caçadores were held in reserve and are left out. The centre had twelve guns, shown as two batteries.",
        "The force had more guns than the list allows for its battalions (one battery per six), which shows as a historical departure.",
